{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.substrate_pair_not_bar_stable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.substrate_pair_not_bar_stable","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.lean#L151-L159","doc":"Neither member of a substrate bar-pair is modulus-stable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.substrate_pair_straddles_unit_circle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.substrate_pair_straddles_unit_circle","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.lean#L138-L149","doc":"**The substrate bar-pair straddles the unit circle.** For real `q > 1` the\nanchor is outside the closed unit ball and its bar-partner is strictly inside.\n\nSo neither member sits on the modulus-fixed locus of\n`bar_modulus_stable_iff_abs_eq_one`, and by\n`not_mem_ball_and_inv_mem_ball` no ball-shaped domain holds both. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.bar_modulus_stable_iff_abs_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.bar_modulus_stable_iff_abs_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.lean#L112-L134","doc":"**A nonzero point is modulus-stable under the bar involution iff it lies on\nthe unit circle.**\n\nThis is the structural reason the Habiro ring is built at roots of unity and not\nat an archimedean anchor: `|q| = 1` is exactly the locus where `q` and `q⁻¹`\nhave the same modulus, so a domain can contain both. Pairs with\n`HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_eq_zero_of_pow_eq_one`, which says the\nevaluation exists there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.bar_pair_not_formable_of_subset_ball","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.bar_pair_not_formable_of_subset_ball","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.lean#L99-L108","doc":"**The obstruction, as used.** If a carrier's domain `S` is contained in the\nopen unit ball, then for every nonzero `q` at most one of `q`, `q⁻¹` lies in `S`.\n\nConsequently `F(q) + F(q⁻¹)` — hence the bar-even and bar-odd projections — is\nnot formable anywhere on `S`. Not divergent: undefined. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.not_mem_ball_and_inv_mem_ball","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.not_mem_ball_and_inv_mem_ball","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.lean#L91-L97","doc":"**The obstruction, pointwise.** For `q ≠ 0`, the point and its bar-partner\nare never both in the open unit ball. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.abs_inv_lt_one_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.abs_inv_lt_one_iff","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/BarInvolutionDomainObstruction.lean#L72-L89","doc":"For a nonzero `q` in a linear ordered field, `|q⁻¹| < 1 ↔ 1 < |q|`.\n\nGeneric per §7c: this is order-and-field content, no archimedean input beyond\nthe ordering itself, so it is stated over `[Field K] [LinearOrder K] [IsStrictOrderedRing K]`\nrather than `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}